# Anti-patterns to Avoid

- Do not resurrect discontinued fixed-price website packages or new digital-business-card sales.
- Do not delete or break existing published cards, mapped domains, orders, admin or onboarding data.
- Do not infer 'unused' from a direct-import scan; account for dynamic imports, CSS assets, runtime scripts, tests and external URLs.
- Do not use arbitrary redesign trends to override approved homepage behavior.
- Do not publish fake or unsourced reviews, client results, prices, guarantees, local offices, speed metrics or conversion statistics.
- Do not blanket-redirect unrelated retired pages to the homepage or advertise non-equivalent hreflang variants.
- Do not force file-splitting solely to satisfy an arbitrary line-count threshold.
- Do not introduce dependencies or services without evaluating their maintenance and security burden.
- Do not treat build success as proof of working routes, SEO tags, accessibility or visual quality.
- Validate typecheck, lint, build and relevant served-build tests; document anything not run.
